  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#2694\", \"PowerToys#15404\", \"PowerToys#37\"], \"answer\": \"Automatic or dynamic tiling in the style of i3, Hyprland or Sway has been requested before. PowerToys#2694 is the main thread. The maintainers closed #37 and #15404 as duplicates of it. Please add your Omarchy, Komorebi and GlazeWM use case there and upvote it, rather than tracking this new ticket. In that thread a maintainer said auto-tile doesn't fit FancyZones' architecture, and that it would work better as a separate module that runs instead of FancyZones. No tiling module exists in PowerToys yet. For now you can use FancyZones with its manual layouts. You can also run a third-party tiling manager such as Komorebi, GlazeWM, FancyWM or Workspacer.\"}",
